  ("1. The pseudopatients feigned a single <b>symptom</b>, but were treated as if the whole illness were present.","<b>symptom</b> (n) — a sign of a disorder. Compare <em>sign</em> (observed by the clinician) and <em>symptom</em> (reported by the patient)."),
  ("2. A diagnosis can become a <b>label</b> that colours how all later behaviour is interpreted.","<b>label</b> (n) — a name that categorises someone and can shape how they are seen. Related: <em>labelling theory</em>."),
